WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.859
(muffled rumbling)

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:02.340
(glass breaking)
(muffled chattering)

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:04.380
- [Noemie] French President
Emmanuel Macron's government

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.900
invoked a special provision
of France's Constitution

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.970
on Thursday to bypass Parliament

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.973
in a bid to push through its
controversial pension reform.

00:00:13.299 --> 00:00:17.799
(Elisabeth speaking foreign language)

00:00:19.169 --> 00:00:20.879
(angry shouting)

00:00:20.879 --> 00:00:23.340
- The move received a frosty
reception in Parliament,

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.721
with lawmakers singing
the national anthem.

00:00:25.721 --> 00:00:28.388
(group singing)

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.060
The use of Article 49 of
the French Constitution

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:39.000
allows the Macron government
to avoid a parliamentary vote

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.324
on the bill, which proposes
raising the retirement age.

00:00:42.324 --> 00:00:44.250
(muffled shouting)

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.020
It comes after public sector workers

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.970
have walked off the job in droves,

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:50.160
culminating in piles of trash building up

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.460
around the French capital.

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:57.030
I'm in Paris with a view
of the iconic Eiffel Tower,

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:58.320
but here's a scene that offers

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.146
a less romantic vision of the city.

00:01:00.146 --> 00:01:03.000
(muffled traffic humming)

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.940
Heaps of trash piled on the city streets.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:09.180
The garbage has not been picked
up in Paris for over a week.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:11.970
This is in response to
the unpopular government

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:13.860
pension overhaul that has been proposed

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:17.420
by French President Emmanuel Macron.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:18.253
(group chanting)

00:01:18.253 --> 00:01:20.670
Macron has proposed
overhauling the pension system.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:23.490
He wants to raise the legal
retirement age by two years

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:25.800
to 64 and make people work longer

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.359
before they can touch their pensions.

00:01:27.359 --> 00:01:28.980
(man shouting in foreign language)

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:31.653
Unions are unhappy with the legislation.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:33.870
- [Noemie] Millions of workers

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:35.610
have gone on strike since January

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:38.447
when the current bill was
first presented to Parliament.

00:01:38.447 --> 00:01:43.447
(group shouting in foreign language)

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:47.190
- [Noemie] Teachers, train
drivers, and oil refinery staff

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:49.050
from across the country are among those

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:50.450
who have joined the strikes.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:55.950
Recent polls showed nearly 70%
of people oppose the reforms,

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:57.780
but Macron says the changes are needed

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:00.150
to protect France's pension
system from collapse

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:03.570
and to maintain control
of government expenditure.

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:05.910
He has pledged to boost military spending

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:08.220
and wants to bring the national deficits

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:11.400
back in line with the
European Union's targets.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.860
France has one of the
lowest rates of retirees

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:17.820
at risk of poverty in Europe,
but this comes at a cost.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.830
France spends close to 15%

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:22.140
of its economic output on pensions.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:24.960
That's almost double what the U.S. spends.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.970
The country's pension system is expected

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:31.970
to run a deficit of 1.8
billion Euros in 2023.

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:37.190
That's set to keep increasing
to 21.2 billion Euros in 2035.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:39.870
As the population ages,
the number of workers

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:42.507
who fund each pension check is shrinking.

00:02:42.507 --> 00:02:44.520
The government has ruled out raising taxes

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:45.660
to sure up deficit,

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:48.385
saying that taxes in
France are already high.

00:02:48.385 --> 00:02:52.718
(Olivier speaking foreign language)

00:03:06.135 --> 00:03:07.849
(muffled shouting)

00:03:07.849 --> 00:03:09.210
- [Noemie] This isn't
the first time Macron

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.760
tried to overhaul France's pension system.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.550
In 2019, he proposed
to streamline France's

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:16.560
42 different state pension plans,

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.720
which vary in retirement age and income,

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:21.120
into one universal system.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.880
He also wanted to introduce
bonuses and penalties

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:27.660
to encourage people to
work until the age of 64.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:30.870
This led to strikes across
the transportation system,

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:32.880
which paralyzed the country for weeks

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.100
before the government shelved its plans

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:37.620
as the COVID-19 pandemic struck,

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:40.020
but some economists say
the proposed changes

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:41.920
won't keep the system afloat for long.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.570
Many see the fights over pension

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:49.696
as the last stand defense of
France's social welfare model.

00:03:49.696 --> 00:03:54.113
(Frederic speaking foreign language)

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:07.440
- [Noemie] France's Senate approved

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.814
the controversial reforms on March 11-

00:04:09.814 --> 00:04:11.520
(official speaking foreign language)

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.590
- [Noemie] But the government
struggled to cobble together

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:15.300
enough votes for it to pass through

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:18.003
the Low House of Parliament,
The National Assembly.

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:22.290
Macron's move comes at
a high political cost.

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:25.350
Protesters in opposition
parties that have painted Macron

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:28.410
as an authoritarian now
have more ammunition

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:30.690
to mobilize the masses.

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:32.229
Demonstrators took to the streets

00:04:32.229 --> 00:04:34.800
after Article 49 was invoked.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:37.170
A number of parties have
said they will retaliate

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:39.753
by putting forward a no confidence motion.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:44.055
If successful, that would
force the government to resign.

00:04:44.055 --> 00:04:48.746
(dramatic tonal music)
(metal clanging)

